---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pagination:
  data: catalog.policies
  size: 1
  alias: policy
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "/policies/{{ policy.slug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  pageId: "policies/{{ policy.slug }}"
  title: "{{ policy.display | safe }} ({{ policy.id }})"
  description: "{{ policy.id }} — {{ policy.display }}.{% if policy.reserved %} Reference number reserved; the policy is not yet drafted.{% else %} Public review draft; not adopted, not in force.{% endif %}"
---
{#-
  One template, two states.

  DRAFTED  — POL-001…010. The reviewed body renders from the repository's own
             markdown, which supplies the page <h1>; nothing is authored here.
  RESERVED — a permanent reference number held for a policy nobody has written
             yet (catalog.js sets `reserved` from the file's canonical_status).
             It renders the export's stub state: the reserved number, an honest
             "not yet drafted" status, a version-history table recording only
             the reservation, and a contact route. No policy content is invented
             to fill it — there is none, and saying so plainly is the point.
             This state supplies its own <h1>, since no markdown body renders.
-#}
{% import "partials/mailto.njk" as mail %}
<header class="titleband">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Uncost</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="/policies/">Policies</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <span>{{ policy.display }}</span></div>
  <div class="meta">
    <span class="pid ref">{{ policy.id }}</span>
    {% if policy.reserved %}
    <span class="status status--planned">Not yet drafted</span>
    <span class="m">Reference reserved</span>
    <span class="m">Last updated: pre-launch</span>
    {% else %}
    <span class="status status--planned">Public review draft &mdash; not in force</span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% if policy.reserved %}
  <h1>{{ policy.display }}</h1>
  {% endif %}
</header>
{% if policy.reserved %}
<div class="pol-wrap">
  <nav class="pol-toc" aria-label="Contents">
    <h2>Contents</h2>
    <a href="#s1">1 &middot; Status</a>
    <a href="#s2">2 &middot; Version history</a>
    <a href="#s3">3 &middot; Contact</a>
  </nav>
  <div class="pol-body">
    <div class="callout">
      <h2 class="s">The plain-language version</h2>
      <p>This policy has not been written. Its reference number is reserved and permanent, so it can be cited now and will still point here once there is something to point at.</p>
    </div>
    <section id="s1">
      <h2 class="s"><span class="num">1</span>Status</h2>
      <p>Not yet drafted. {{ policy.id }} is held in the public record as a reserved reference. There is no policy text, no scope and no rules &mdash; nothing here is in force, and a reserved reference is not an adopted policy.</p>
      <p>Drafting it means writing it against the controlling source recorded in <a href="https://github.com/uncost-org/uncost/blob/main/docs/CONTROL.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs/CONTROL.md</a>, stamping its derivation, adding it to the policy pack, and moving its status to draft &mdash; the same route every other policy took. Until then, do not cite this page as authority for anything.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="s2">
      <h2 class="s"><span class="num">2</span>Version history</h2>
      <table class="vhist">
        <thead><tr><th class="w-90">Version</th><th class="w-150">Date</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>&mdash;</td><td>Pre-launch</td><td>Reference number reserved. Drafting not started.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section id="s3">
      <h2 class="s"><span class="num">3</span>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this reservation? Email {{ mail.email() }}. The full policy set is on the <a href="/policies/">Policies</a> page, and the reserved file itself is in the <a href="https://github.com/uncost-org/uncost/blob/main/policies/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">public repository</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
{% else %}
<article class="prose-60">
{{ policy.body | md | safe }}
</article>
{% endif %}
